                  <msItem>
                     <title>Fragmenta polyphonica (14 fols)</title>
                     <note type="MLGB3_generalNotes">Lat. liturg. d.20 consists of leaves removed
                        from the medieval bindings of Worcester Cathedral manuscripts in the
                        Bodleian (fols 12–19, 22–25, 34, 35) and photographs of leaves in (a) the
                        binding of BL, Add. 25031 and in (b) a guardbook at Worcester Cathedral (MS
                        Add. 68). These leaves come from at least three, but perhaps not more than
                        three, volumes of polyphonic music: (a) fols 1-22, used in BL, Add. 25031;
                        Bodleian, Auct. F.inf.1.3, and Hatton 30; and Worcester Cathedral, F.34,
                        125, 133, Q.31; (b) fols 22-35, used in Bodleian, Bodley 862; Oxford,
                        Magdalen College, lat. 100; and Worcester Cathedral, Q.72; (c) fols 36-39,
                        used in an unidentified binding, possibly Worcester Cathedral, Q.21. See A.
                        Hughes, Worcester Medieval Harmony; L. A. Dittmer, The Worcester Fragments
                        (1957).</note>
                  </msItem>
               </msContents>
